    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1 Number of analysis reports regarding the current situation of the destination with sustainable tourism development and promoting energy efficiency perspective
2.1 Number of green destination  models
2.2 Number of new initiatives on promoting energy efficiency in pilot destination
2.3 Number of tourism actors that integrated at least one energy efficiency application and/or use of renewable energy resources.
3.1 Number of trainings provided on energy efficiency and use of renewable energy resources.
3.2 Number of trainings provided on ecological sustainability, responsible consumption and production, sustainable tourism etc. 
3.3 Number of people participated to trainings on Energy Managers and on  Energy Management System Consultancy
3.4 Number of workshops organized 
3.5 Number of innovative project ideas to be supported on promoting energy efficiency in tourism 
3.6 Number of awareness raising activities  
4.1 Number of networking and visibility activities</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Baseline: N/A</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Destination based strategy and roadmap on a) sustainable consumption and production b) strategy and roadmap on environmentally friendly transportation systems c) green procurement and supply chain management
2. At least 10 local tourism initiatives (at least 50% women-run and or family businesses where women are active) changed their way of doing business and integrated at least one energy efficiency application and/or use of renewable energy resources.
3.At least 5 trainings for tourism business and local people on ecological sustainability, responsible consumption and production, sustainable tourism etc.
4.At least 5 trainings for tourism business and local people on energy efficiency
5. At least 10 people (%50 will be women) will participate energy audit trainings</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Green destination standards revieweed in different countries and those that can be adapted to K&#xfc;&#xe7;&#xfc;kk&#xf6;y was identified
Roadmaps on green purchasing, sustainable transportation, sustainable production and consumption.
Eenergy audits in small-scale tourism enterprises in K&#xfc;&#xe7;&#xfc;kk&#xf6;y and proposed solutions to reduce energy consumption and increase energy efficiency. 
Trainings to tourism enterprises on energy efficiency in tourism, sustainable tourism and green destinations, and to students on different topics ranging from energy efficiency to tourism, waste management to climate change, SDGs to gender equality. 
Alternative hiking and cycling routes as well as an energy route in and around K&#xfc;&#xe7;&#xfc;kk&#xf6;y, and placed signboards including qualified maps to enable visitors to experience touristic values.
Gender Equality Action Plan was prepared to guide the work carried out. 
Energy manager trainings to get certification and become capable of conducting energy audits, thereby increasing employment in this field.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
